          "message": {
            "text": "The ordinary-Latin control now asserts that even a formerly non-routed run has shapesWithHarfbuzz=true. Focused routing/text tests pass; the full 3,704-test suite had one pre-existing SF Pro fallback-order assertion that passes focused and is unrelated to shaping consolidation.",
            "markdown": "The ordinary-Latin control now asserts that even a formerly non-routed run has shapesWithHarfbuzz=true. Focused routing/text tests pass; the full 3,704-test suite had one pre-existing SF Pro fallback-order assertion that passes focused and is unrelated to shaping consolidation."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/harfbuzz-run-routing.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 108,
                  "endLine": 121,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n  it(\"routes ordinary Latin too, and never double-wraps an hb font\", () => {\n    const key = resolveFontKey(\"Arial Unicode MS\");\n    const primary = getFontInstance(key, 400, 16, 0)!;\n    const latin = splitArabic(\"hello\");\n    expect(latin[0].font === primary).toBe(false);\n    expect(latin[0].font.shapesWithHarfbuzz).toBe(true);\n    // A font already shaping through HarfBuzz (here: the feature-list proxy)\n    // must come back unchanged — a proxy-over-proxy has no `getGlyph` and\n    // would silently swap the outline engine.\n    const featProxy = fontFeatureValueShapingOverride(primary, key, 400, 16, 0, undefined, [\"-liga\"]);\n    expect(featProxy === primary).toBe(false);\n    expect(harfbuzzShapedRunOverride(featProxy, key, 400, 16, 0, undefined, \"مرحبا\") === featProxy).toBe(true);\n  });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
